", "start": 40.513, "end": 40.662}, {"text": "wrong", "start": 40.662, "end": 41.025}, {"text": "in", "start": 41.025, "end": 41.15}, {"text": "either", "start": 41.15, "end": 41.4}, {"text": "direction", "start": 41.4, "end": 42.062}, {"text": "and", "start": 42.062, "end": 42.188}, {"text": "you'll", "start": 42.188, "end": 42.362}, {"text": "feel", "start": 42.362, "end": 42.587}, {"text": "it", "start": 42.587, "end": 42.7}, {"text": "for", "start": 42.7, "end": 42.862}, {"text": "years", "start": 42.862, "end": 43.625}]}, {"index": 4, "kind": "prose", "text": "The analogy: a monolith is one big restaurant kitchen — every cook in one room, shouting distance from everyone else. Communication is instant, but Thanksgiving dinner for 400 means chaos in a single space. Microservices are a food court — each stall independent, with its own staff, menu, and hours. One stall's grease fire doesn't close the others, but now you need shared plumbing, shared seating, and a directory so customers can find the dumplings.", "start": 43.875, "end": 71.225, "words": [{"text": "The", "start": 44.125, "end": 44.25}, {"text": "analogy", "start": 44.25, "end": 44.975}, {"text": "a", "start": 44.975, "end": 45.2}, {"text": "monolith", "start": 45.2, "end": 45.725}, {"text": "is", "start": 45.725, "end": 45.888}, {"text": "one", "start": 45.888, "end": 46.188}, {"text": "big", "start": 46.188, "end": 46.425}, {"text": "restaurant", "start": 46.425, "end": 46.8}, {"text": "kitchen", "start": 46.8, "end": 47.413}, {"text": "every", "start": 47.413, "end": 47.8}, {"text": "cook", "start": 47.8, "end": 48.013}, {"text": "in", "start": 48.013, "end": 48.15}, {"text": "one", "start": 48.15, "end": 48.375}, {"text": "room", "start": 48.375, "end": 48.775}, {"text": "shouting", "start": 48.775, "end": 49.25}, {"text": "distance", "start": 49.25, "end": 49.675}, {"text": "from", "start": 49.675, "end": 49.825}, {"text": "everyone", "start": 49.825, "end": 50.188}, {"text": "else", "start": 50.1