art": 151.05, "end": 151.95}]}, {"index": 11, "kind": "prose", "text": "The flip side: if you have five genuinely independent teams stepping on each other in one repo, splitting is how you stop the merge-conflict wars. Architecture follows org, not the other way around.", "start": 152.2, "end": 164.85, "words": [{"text": "The", "start": 152.45, "end": 152.537}, {"text": "flip", "start": 152.537, "end": 152.837}, {"text": "side", "start": 152.837, "end": 153.45}, {"text": "if", "start": 153.45, "end": 153.688}, {"text": "you", "start": 153.688, "end": 153.775}, {"text": "have", "start": 153.775, "end": 154.0}, {"text": "five", "start": 154.0, "end": 154.45}, {"text": "genuinely", "start": 154.45, "end": 154.975}, {"text": "independent", "start": 154.975, "end": 155.55}, {"text": "teams", "start": 155.55, "end": 156.037}, {"text": "stepping", "start": 156.037, "end": 156.387}, {"text": "on", "start": 156.387, "end": 156.487}, {"text": "each", "start": 156.487, "end": 156.662}, {"text": "other", "start": 156.662, "end": 156.95}, {"text": "in", "start": 156.95, "end": 157.1}, {"text": "one", "start": 157.1, "end": 157.325}, {"text": "repo", "start": 157.325, "end": 158.0}, {"text": "splitting", "start": 158.0, "end": 158.65}, {"text": "is", "start": 158.65, "end": 158.8}, {"text": "how", "start": 158.8, "end": 159.0}, {"text": "you", "start": 159.0, "end": 159.162}, {"text": "stop", "start": 159.162, "end": 159.525}, {"text": "the", "start": 159.525, "end": 159.65}, {"text": "merge", "start": 159.65, "end": 160.475}, {"text": "conflict", "start": 160.475, "end": 160.475}, {"text": "wars", "start": 160.475, "end": 161.4}, {"text": "Architecture", "start": 161.4, "end": 162.225}, {"text": "follows", "start": 162.225, "end": 162.6}, {"text": "org", "start": 162.6, "end": 163.075}, {"text": "not", "start": 163.075, "end": 163.387}, {"text": "the", "start": 163.387, "end": 163.462}, {"text": "other", "start": 163.462, "end": 163.675}, {"text": "way", "start": 163.675, "end": 163.85}, {"text": "around", "start": 163.85, "end": 164.6}]}, {"index": 12, "kind": "prose", "text": "The distributed monolith: the worst of both", "start": 164.85, "end": 167.9, "words": [{"text": "The", "start": 165.1, "end": 165.175}, {"text": "distributed", "start": 165.175, "end": 165.825}, {"text": "monolith", "start": 165.825, "end": 166.475}, {"text": "the", "start": 166.475, "end": 166.7}, {"text": "worst", "start": 166.7, "end": 167.012}, {"text": "of", "start": 167.012, "end": 167.1}, {"text": "both", "start": 167.1, "end": 167.65}]}, {"index": 13, "kind": "prose", "text": "The failure mode to fear has a name: the distributed monolith. It looks like microservices (many deployables, network calls everywhere) but behaves like a monolith (everything must deploy together, one service's change breaks five others, no independent scaling). You get all the operational pain of distribution with none of the autonomy. Telltale signs: distributed transactions across services, lockstep deployments, and a \"service\" diagram that is really one big ball of mud with HTTP in the middle.", "start": 167.9, "end": 200.675, "words": [{"text": "The", "start": 168.15, "end": 168.263}, {"text": "failure", "start": 168.263, "end": 168.75}, {"text": "mode", "start": 168.75, "end": 169.025}, {"text": "to", "start": 169.025, "end": 169.162}, {"text": "fear", "start": 169.162, "end": 169.475}, {"text": "has", "start": 169.475, "end": 169.638}, {"text": "a", "start": 169.638, "end": 169.7}, {"text": "name", "start": 169.7, "end": 170.325}, {"text": "the", "start": 170.325, "end": 170.525}, {"text": "distributed", "start": 170.525, "end": 171.2}, {"text": "monolith", "start": 171.2, "end": 172.075}, {"text": "It", "start": 172.075, "end": 172.325}, {"text": "looks", "start": 172.325, "end": 172.575}, {"text": "like", "start": 172.575, "end": 172.8}, {"text": "microservices", "start": 172.8, "end": 173.963}, {"text": "many", "start": 173.963, "end": 174.25}, {"text": "deployables", "st